<SiteLayout
  title="About The Dead Air Archive"
  description="Learn how to read The Dead Air Archive, a literary paranormal-horror project presented through interconnected stories and records."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>About The Dead Air Archive</h1>

      <p>
        The Dead Air Archive is a literary paranormal-horror project presented as an
        interconnected collection of stories and records.
      </p>

      <p>
        Each story follows people attempting to document events that resist a single
        explanation. Case summaries, character records, locations, objects, and open mysteries
        allow readers to trace what happened, compare accounts, and follow connections across the
        archive.
      </p>

      <h2>How to Read the Archive</h2>

      <p>
        Begin with the <a href="/stories/">Stories</a> section. After reading a story, follow its
        linked records to examine the people involved, the evidence collected, the objects placed
        into custody, and the questions that remain unresolved.
      </p>

      <p>
        The records expand the stories without providing a final authoritative explanation.
        Testimony may conflict. Evidence may remain incomplete. Ordinary explanations and
        paranormal interpretations can exist beside one another.
      </p>

      <h2>Fiction and Reported Material</h2>

      <p>The Dead Air Archive is a work of fiction.</p>

      <p>
        Some stories are based on reported paranormal-investigation accounts. Events, characters,
        locations, and identifying details may be fictionalized. Raw source materials, private
        identities, restricted participant information, and internal development records are not
        included in the public archive.
      </p>

      <h2>The Archive’s Approach</h2>

      <p>
        The project draws on incident reports, evidence logs, institutional records, oral
        testimony, and documentary-horror traditions. Its visual design evokes basement archives,
        aging files, and oxidized identification plates while keeping the text quiet and legible.
      </p>

      <p>
        The archive records what people experienced, what the available evidence supports, and
        where certainty ends.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
